.TH DOCKER-HELPER 1
.SH NAME
docker-helper \- Policy-enforcing Docker mediation daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docker-helper
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.BI "COMMAND"
[\& ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docker-helper
is a policy-enforcing daemon that provides a restricted interface to Docker.
It mediates Docker operations for coding agents running on the same machine,
restricting host path access to session workspaces and enforcing policy on
build, pull, and run operations.
.PP
Deployment mode is determined by effective UID:
.IP \(bu 4
\fIUser mode\fR (non-root): Private Unix socket, per-user configuration
.IP \(bu 4
\fISystem mode\fR (root): System Unix socket + loopback HTTP, system-wide configuration
.SH DEPLOYMENT MODES
.SS User Mode
Runs as the current user. Configuration at
.IR ~/.config/docker-helper/config.json ,
state at
.IR ~/.local/state/docker-helper .
No AppArmor integration.
.SS System Mode
Runs as root. Configuration at
.IR /etc/docker-helper/config.json ,
state at
.IR /var/lib/docker-helper .
AppArmor confinement with managed workspace roots.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS General Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper serve
Start the HTTP server (daemon mode).
.TP
.B docker-helper init [\-\-allowed-root PATH]
Initialize configuration and admin token. In system mode, the initial
allowed_root is added to managed AppArmor roots. Subsequent changes to
configuration or principal allowed roots do NOT automatically update AppArmor;
use \fIdocker-helper apparmor root\fR to manage them.
.TP
.B docker-helper reload [\-\-system | \-\-endpoint URL | \-\-token-file FILE]
Reload configuration. Use \fB\-\-system\fR for system daemon, \fB\-\-endpoint\fR
or \fB\-\-token-file\fR for user daemon.
.TP
.B docker-helper version
Print version information.
.TP
.B docker-helper help [COMMAND]
Show help for a command.
.SS Session Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper session create [\-\-workspace PATH]
Create a session for a workspace.
.TP
.B docker-helper session list
List active sessions.
.TP
.B docker-helper session remove SESSION
Remove a session.
.SS Config Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper config show
Show current configuration.
.TP
.B docker-helper config edit
Edit configuration interactively.
.SS Principal Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper principal allowed-root add PATH
Add an allowed root for a principal.
.TP
.B docker-helper principal allowed-root remove PATH
Remove an allowed root.
.TP
.B docker-helper principal allowed-root list
List allowed roots.
.SS Credential Commands
.TP
.B docker-helper credential issue SESSION
Issue a session credential.
.TP
.B docker-helper credential validate TOKEN
Validate a session token.
.SS AppArmor Commands (System Mode)
.TP
.B docker-helper apparmor root add PATH
Add a workspace root to managed AppArmor policy.
.TP
.B docker-helper apparmor root remove PATH
Remove a workspace root.
.TP
.B docker-helper apparmor root list
List managed workspace roots.
.TP
.B docker-helper apparmor reload
Reload AppArmor profile.
.SH OPERATOR ENDPOINT SELECTION
For reload and credential commands, select the target daemon via:
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-system\fR: System daemon (requires root)
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-endpoint URL\fR: HTTP endpoint URL
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-token-file FILE\fR: Token file for authentication
.PP
Local system mode uses Unix socket + loopback HTTP (127.0.0.1:52375 default).
No remote or TLS support in Release 2.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Operational or runtime failure
.TP
.B 2
Invalid CLI arguments or input
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/docker-helper/config.json
System mode configuration
.TP
.B /etc/docker-helper/admin.token
System mode admin token
.TP
.B /var/lib/docker-helper/docker-helper.db
System mode state database
.TP
.B /run/docker-helper/docker-helper.sock
System mode Unix socket
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docker-helper/config.json
User mode configuration
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/docker-helper
User mode state directory
.SH SECURITY
.IP \(bu 4
.B docker-helper
mediates Docker access; rootful Docker access is root-equivalent host capability
.IP \(bu 4
Credentials and session tokens are capabilities—protect them accordingly
.IP \(bu 4
AppArmor confinement restricts filesystem and capability access
.IP \(bu 4
No remote or non-loopback network access in Release 2
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker-helper-config (5),
.BR apparmor (7)
